<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan MFIG buys 56-60,000T US corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan MFIG buys 56-60,000T US corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Members Feed Industry Group bought a 56,000-tonne shipment of U.S. No.2 corn, with an option for an additional 4,000 tonnes, from Toepfer at a tender on Wednesday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The feed group's main buyers are Taiwan's Formosa Oilseed, Fomau Cereal, Morn Sun Feed Mill and Shin Tai Industry.</p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Tonnage    Date/Location</p>
<p>		U.S. Gulf  Pacific N.W.    Prices</p>
<p> 56-60,000  Sept 7-21  Sept 22-Oct 6   $121.00</p>
<p>-- Taipei newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
